	quests: [
		{
			title: "Hunt and Scavenge"
			x: -8.75d
			y: 0.25d
			shape: "hexagon"
			subtitle: "Digging Through the Cabinets"
			description: [
				"&dNow that you are Level 20, Bandit, a bunch of new things have opened up for you. The first of these is a new Objective type for the vaults : Scavenger."
				""
				"&5Scavenger is probably one of the most difficult objectives, and its Completion Crate is the most...lucrative to match it."
				""
				"&dOther than a blackout in Bingo at least."
				""
				"&5Ain't sure Bandit is ready for that yet. "
				""
				"&dMaybe, maybe not. But right now we're talking about Scav Vaults! In these, you get a list of items you need to find in THAT vault specifically. They'll be at the top of your screen, with an icon of where to find them: from either chests, monsters, or ores."
				""
				"&5Get all of em, Bandit, and find a Scavenger Altar (green glowing altar that spawns in most rooms). Right Click each stack to deposit it before the timer runs out."
				""
				"&dIf ya don't get enough in time, you'll want to leave via the Portal before the time runs out, Bandit."
			]
			dependencies: ["148669A61C9EFBF4"]
			hide: true
			id: "1881243BF68F0FAC"
			tasks: [{
				id: "288CE78D02906B90"
				type: "woldsvaults:vault_level"
				title: "Reach Level 20"
				icon: "the_vault:scavenger_altar"
				value: 20
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "6F0925C1B31FC8B5"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:crystal_seal_hunter"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Vendor Door"
			x: -9.25d
			y: 1.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Vendoor: Capitalism, Ho!"
			description: [
				"&dThere are two kinds of doors that will start spawning in the Vaults after level 20, Bandit."
				""
				"&5Vendoors lead to special rooms that have Vendor Pedestals in them. These doors spawn on the walls inside Vault Rooms, usually on the bottom floor."
				""
				"&dThere's a variety of things the Vendor Pedestals can sell, Bandit, some of them only findable in Vendoor rooms."
				""
				"&5Money is Vault Gold, and the Pedestal will pull it directly from your Wallet or Pouches."
				""
				"&dYou can get a discount on Vendor Pedestals with a certain Expertise."
				""
				"&5Oh! Also, Bandit, keep yer eyes open. Some of the Vendor rooms have some hidden loot in em."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["1881243BF68F0FAC"]
			id: "4905625BD3C4B3C4"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4947C4D29A9DB40A"
				type: "observation"
				title: "Find a Vendoor"
				icon: "the_vault:vendor_door"
				timer: 0L
				observe_type: 0
				to_observe: "the_vault:vendor_door"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "5A4EC26D95463661"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "The \"True\" Hunt"
			x: -6.75d
			y: 0.25d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "Artifacts 5 by 5"
			description: [
				"&dNow that you are level 20, Bandit, you'll start finding Unidentified Artifacts in your Completion Crates."
				""
				"&5They'll also occasionally show up in the Black Market. And maybe the Bounty table, I've not seen that myself though."
				""
				"&dEither way, the FOP give Users and Power Users a way to 'win' : Collect all 25 Artifacts, complete the 'tapestry', and defeat the final boss."
				""
				"&5The Herald is it's name, apparently. It's the avatar of the CEO of FOP."
				""
				"&dFor Power Users, the FOP tell them this is their only way to freedom. But there's a bit of a catch, Bandit."
				""
				"&5You will never obtain all 25 artifacts. The game is rigged from the start."
				""
				"&dBut heck to that. We have a while before we can truely start modifying things around the artifacts, its a fairly controlled system. But not invincible."
			]
			dependencies: ["1881243BF68F0FAC"]
			id: "2EC8B80AE1A271D5"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0E348B08B753AA85"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:artifact_projector_block"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "57FE043DE4C905F7"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Inscribing a Path"
			icon: "the_vault:vault_catalyst_infused"
			x: -6.25d
			y: 2.5d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Determined Destiny"
			description: [
				"&dBandit, it seems at around level 24 you'll start finding Catalyst fragments in Gilded Chests."
				""
				"&524? What an odd level..."
				""
				"&dRight? Bandit, Catalyst fragments can be combined, and then brought into a Catalyst Infusion Table and turned into something useful."
				""
				"&5Infused Catalysts can be applied to your Vault Crystal (in the Crystal Workbench, of course), and can increase the amount of chests you get, or coins, or other useful things."
				""
				"&dOh, the notes here say you can only find them in unmodified Vaults. Apparently now that means 'any vault with 2 or less Catalysts applied to it'."
				""
				"&5I guess that's good to know. Oh! Almost forgot to tell him, sis. We've snuck in a new kind of 'blind' box into the FOP loot pools : The Catalyst Box. Obvious what is in it, of course."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["2EC8B80AE1A271D5"]
			id: "46082D6F0590EDD4"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "3ECECEB3891A0EE3"
					type: "item"
					item: "the_vault:catalyst_infusion_table"
				}
				{
					id: "40B665B067EE0A96"
					type: "item"
					item: "the_vault:vault_catalyst_fragment"
				}
			]
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "2DC40071E3BCF9F5"
					type: "choice"
					table_id: 5632731352558517809L
				}
				{
					id: "2D49A7C4C483B355"
